From f9e4c93ae012504791e0f386a42d998bb12af978 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kyle Zhang <kelzhan@google.com>
Date: Fri, 26 Jun 2026 19:26:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] Fix race conditions in CryptoHal plugin usage

The previous implementation of `decrypt` and `getKeyHandle` unlocked
`mLock` while `mPlugin` could be concurrently reset by
`destroyPlugin()`. This created a window for use-after-free or null
dereference when the plugin was dispatched. Additionally, the manual
unlock within the `Mutex::Autolock` scope caused double-unlocking
undefined behavior upon scope exit.

This commit scopes the `Autolock` explicitly and takes a strong reference
of the plugin under the lock. This ensures safe dispatch of the IPC and
avoids duplicate unlocks, mitigating the TOCTOU issue.

Bug: 503553199
Test: build libmediadrm
Flag: EXEMPT BUGFIX
Cherrypick-From: https://googleplex-android-review.googlesource.com/q/commit:07833af6498d65a0f2dc520f6be6ee8ca2c80967
